    "The LCS1269 record is a predicted HIA-based value rather than a measured absolute bioavailability.",
    "Vinorelbine bioavailability is formulation-dependent, and the query formulation is unspecified.",
    "First-pass metabolism and systemic clearance of the query are not experimentally characterized."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L4 adds only permeability and solubility records for CP-25, vinpocetine, compound 8, and paclitaxel; none are query-specific or close enough to override the transferable analog evidence from vinorelbine (~40%), LCS1269 (predicted >30%), and ondansetron (50–65%). No affirmative threshold-relevant low-F evidence applies to the query, so the high prediction is kept with moderate confidence."
}

